1,0$Diversity of species of the genus Conocybe on dung from Punjab, India///Amandeep, Atri, Munruchi ///Mycosphere 6(1): 19–42(2015)
1,0$


 µm 
1,2 $ Stipe cuticle mainly consisting of lecythiform caulocystidia; non-lecythiform caulocystidia absent or very rarely present; pseudoparaphyses absent in the hymenophore
1,6 $ Stipe cuticle consists of a mixture of lecythiform and non-lecythiform caulocystidia or only non-lecythiform caulocystidia; pseudoparaphyses absent or present between basidia in the hymenophore
2,3 $ Pileocystidia present; stipe equal in diameter throughout
2,5 $ Pileocystidia absent; stipe base obclavate
3,0 $ Ammonia reaction positive, long, needle-shaped crystals are produced in ammonical mounts of the lamellae; pileus reddish brown when young, brownish yellow with reddish brown apex at maturity; lamellae adnate, subdistant; basidiospores 8.5-10.7 × 5.7-6.4 µm $ C. brachypodii
3,4 $ Ammonia reaction negative
4,0 $ Pileus reddish golden when young, light brown at maturity, smooth, umbonate; lamellae distant; caulocystidia exclusively lecythiform.. $ C. subxerophytica var. subxerophytica
4,0 $ Pileus yellowish brown to dark brown, radially wrinkled, ex-umbonate; lamellae subdistant; caulocystidia mainly lecythiform, but mixed with few non-lecythiform elements $ C. subxerophytica var. brunnea
5,0 $ Lamellae adnexed, 3-sized; stipe surface white, brownish when handled; basidiospores 12-15 × 6.8-8.5 µm ; cheilocystidia 17-22 × 3.4-7.6 (8.5) µm $ C. leucopus
5,0 $ Lamellae adnate, 2-sized; stipe surface yellowish white, unchanging; basidiospores 8.5-12 × 5-7 µm ; cheilocystidia 22-32.3 × 6.8-9.3 µm $ C. magnicapitata
6,7 $ Pseudoparaphyses absent
6,15 $ Pseudoparaphyses present
7,8 $ Caulocystidia mixed, both lecythiform and non-lecythiform
7,9 $ Caulocystidia exclusively non-lecythiform
8,0 $ Pileus 3-3.3 cm broad, campanulate to conico-convex, with an elongated brown umbo, surface yellowish brown with lighter margin, bruising brown; basidia 4-spored $ C. subpubescens
8,0 $ Pileus 1-1.4 cm broad, conical, with slightly raised apex, surface reddish brown; basidia 2-, 3- and 4-spored $ C. uralensis
9,0 $ Stipe tubular, base elongated to form a pseudorrhiza; pileus surface yellowish brown having white shades, with small point like brown umbo; basidia 2- and 4-spored; basidiospores 10-12.7 × 6.8-8.5 µm , limoniform-subhexagonal in face view, ellipsoidal in side view; lecythiform pileocystidia present $ C. microrrhiza var. coprophila
9,10 $ Stipe with equal or bulbous base, pseudorrhiza absent; pileocystidia present or absent
10,0 $ Carpophores 6-16 cm in height; pileus surface pale white, pale gray along the periphery, conical with elongated yellowish brown umbo, pileal margin striate-plicate, with radiating ridges and grooves extending up to the apex; stipe with distinctly bulbous base; basidiospores 10-17 × 7.6-10 µm ; clamp connections absent throughout $ C. apala
10,11 $ Pileus conical to campanulate, pileal margin never plicate, never with ridges and grooves; clamp connections present in stipe context hyphae
11,12 $ Pileal margin distinctly striate
11,13 $ Pileal margin always non-striate
12,0 $ Pileus surface grayish white to pale gray, grayish brown at maturity, 1.2-1.3 cm broad; lamellae adnate; stipe cylindrical; pileocystidia absent; caulocystidia sometimes with loops at the apex $ C. moseri
12,0 $ Pileus surface brownish orange when young, grayish yellow, 1.7-2.4 cm broad; lamellae adnexed; stipe with bulbous base; pileocystidia present; caulocystidia without loops $ C. velutipes
13,0 $ Pileus umbonate, surface yellowish brown, dark brown towards the margin; basidia 4-spored; basidiospores 10-12.8 (13.5) × 5.7-7 µm , lentiform in face view $ C. lenticulospora
13,14 $ Pileus ex-umbonate; basidia 2- and 4-spored
14,0 $ Pileus beige, creamish when young, reddish brown at maturity; pileocystidia absent; basidia mostly 4-spored; basidiospores 10-12.8 (13.5) × 6-7.6 µm $ C. fuscimarginata
14,0 $ Pileus yellowish brown; pileocystidia present, sometimes with loops at the apex; basidia mostly 2-spored; basidiospores 12-15.3 (16) × 7.5-9.3 µm $ C. rickenii
15,0 $ Pileus conical, ex-umbonate, with non-striate margin, surface pale to light creamish when young, yellowish brown at maturity; lamellae adnate, with hard and wrinkled edges at maturity; stipe 0.2-0.3 cm broad; basidia mostly 2-spored $ C. crispa
15,0 $ Pileus conical to convex, umbonate, with striate, sometimes reflexed margin, surface white; lamellae adnexed to free, with smooth edges; stipe 0.3-0.5 cm broad; basidia 4-spored $ C. albipes
